1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,270
Hello everyone, I'm Ria!

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:08,950
Everyone, do you happen to know about MBTI?

3
00:00:08,950 --> 00:00:13,680
MBTI is a personality test.

4
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:20,300
Korean people really love MBTI.

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:25,210
When people meet for the first time, they say this.

6
00:00:25,210 --> 00:00:28,320
"What is your MBTI?"

7
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:41,280
People talk about MBTI a lot when making friends, on blind dates, and even at work.

8
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,370
It's a trend.

9
00:00:43,370 --> 00:00:51,680
People use MBTI to have small talk.

10
00:00:51,680 --> 00:01:02,710
So today, I'm going to explain Korea's MBTI culture in an easy way.

11
00:01:02,710 --> 00:01:10,070
And let's also learn some Korean expressions about personality.

12
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:14,120
Please listen carefully.

13
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:21,750
There are so many questions in the MBTI test.

14
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:33,080
There are a lot, but I'll tell you just the key, the core points.

15
00:01:33,080 --> 00:01:40,830
Listen to this and try testing your personality too.

16
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:44,180
Here are the letters.

17
00:01:44,180 --> 00:01:49,590
First, it's E and I.

18
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:56,510
E likes people. They like going outside.

19
00:01:56,510 --> 00:02:02,240
They get energy when they meet friends.

20
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:10,750
For example, let's say you worked hard during the weekdays.

21
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,550
You worked.

22
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:19,600
It was very tiring, but you go out again on the weekend.

23
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:21,220
You go out.

24
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:24,060
You don't get exhausted.

25
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:30,530
You meet friends and talk at a cafe.

26
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,080
Noraebang (Karaoke).

27
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:34,680
You go to noraebang too.

28
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:39,190
Then you feel good.

29
00:02:39,190 --> 00:02:42,270
This is E.

30
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:49,820
Rather, they feel good after meeting people.

31
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,080
They feel better.

32
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:56,590
They get energized.

33
00:02:56,590 --> 00:03:04,320
On the other hand, I likes being alone more.

34
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:07,100
They like being home.

35
00:03:07,100 --> 00:14:01,010
They like being inside more than outside.
36
00:14:01,010 --> 00:03:19,040
They get energy when they are alone.

36
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:23,020
Their energy gets recharged.

37
00:03:23,020 --> 00:03:31,230
They feel more comfortable with fewer people than many people.

38
00:03:31,230 --> 00:03:38,820
For example, they quietly watch a movie at home.

39
00:03:38,820 --> 00:03:42,500
They watch videos.

40
00:03:42,500 --> 00:03:44,530
They play games.

41
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:47,840
They are happy when they read books.

42
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:51,070
This is I.

43
00:03:51,070 --> 00:04:00,100
In Korea, people ask "Are you an E or an I?" very often.

44
00:04:00,100 --> 00:04:02,910
What are you?

45
00:04:02,910 --> 00:04:10,490
When I took this test, I got almost half and half.

46
00:04:10,490 --> 00:04:12,170
Half and half.

47
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:24,040
So I like being alone, and I also really like talking with people.

48
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:26,040
It's interesting, right?

49
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:37,120
There is a sure way to distinguish between E and I.

50
00:04:37,120 --> 00:04:39,550
A sure way.

51
00:04:39,550 --> 00:04:45,170
Listen to this and think about it.

52
00:04:45,170 --> 00:04:55,030
Suppose you are so tired that you are resting at home.

53
00:04:55,030 --> 00:04:57,020
You want to sleep.

54
00:04:57,020 --> 00:05:03,810
But suddenly, a friend contacts you.

55
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:08,770
They contact you even though you didn't make plans.

56
00:05:08,770 --> 00:05:21,150
"Hey, where are you? I'm... in your neighborhood, near your house. Come out!"

57
00:05:21,150 --> 00:05:25,310
How do you feel?

58
00:05:25,310 --> 00:05:30,260
How would you answer?

59
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:35,440
Pause for a moment and think.

60
00:05:35,440 --> 00:05:42,830
E's are so happy that they go to meet the friend right away.

61
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:50,010
I's want to rest at home, so they don't want to go out.

62
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:53,390
Next are N and S.

63
00:05:53,390 --> 00:05:58,800
N likes to imagine things.

64
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:03,440
They like talking about the future.

65
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:05,890
They are creative.

66
00:06:05,890 --> 00:06:07,800
To be creative.

67
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,710
They are creative.

68
00:06:09,710 --> 00:06:13,020
They have many ideas.

69
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:19,110
For example, "What if I go to space?"

70
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:27,630
"What if I become a zombie?" They think like this a lot.

71
00:06:27,630 --> 00:06:30,270
They imagine a lot.

72
00:06:30,270 --> 00:06:33,020
This is N.

73
00:06:33,020 --> 00:06:37,530
S, on the contrary, is realistic.

74
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,170
To be realistic.

75
00:06:39,170 --> 00:06:41,020
They are realistic.

76
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:46,020
They don't like "What if..." questions.

77
00:06:46,020 --> 00:06:52,450
Right now, this moment is the most important.

78
00:06:52,450 --> 00:06:57,660
They like facts more than imagination.

79
00:06:57,660 --> 00:06:59,070
Facts.

80
00:06:59,070 --> 00:07:07,100
For example, "What should I eat today? Did the stocks go up?"

81
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:11,760
They talk about these realistic things a lot.

82
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:13,880
This is S.

83
00:07:13,880 --> 00:07:15,780
How about you?

84
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:23,090
I was half and half between E and I earlier, right?

85
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:27,470
I'm not half and half in this part.

86
00:07:27,470 --> 00:07:31,070
One side is very, very strong.

87
00:07:31,070 --> 00:07:32,540
What could it be?

88
00:07:32,540 --> 00:07:35,780
Am I an N or an S?

89
00:07:35,780 --> 00:07:49,410
Anyway, in Korea, conversation can be a bit difficult if N and S are different.

90
00:07:49,410 --> 00:07:51,840
So it's fun.

91
00:07:51,840 --> 00:07:54,620
Next are T and F.

92
00:07:54,620 --> 00:08:02,780
This part is the most important when having small talk in Korean.

93
00:08:02,780 --> 00:08:10,110
I'll ask a question before I explain.

94
00:08:10,110 --> 00:08:11,980
Question!

95
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:18,370
This is a very famous question in Korea.

96
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:26,990
Everyone, I was so sad yesterday that I bought bread.

97
00:08:26,990 --> 00:08:30,180
Bread! I bought bread.

98
00:08:30,180 --> 00:08:35,800
Pause for a moment and think about it.

99
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:39,810
I was so sad that I bought bread.

100
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:43,870
Try answering very honestly.

101
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:48,560
Now, let me explain.

102
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:55,440
T values logic and thoughts.

103
00:08:55,440 --> 00:08:58,390
They are very logical.

104
00:08:58,390 --> 00:08:59,840
To be logical.

105
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,750
They are logical.

106
00:09:01,750 --> 00:09:05,890
And they speak honestly.

107
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:15,010
If a friend says, "I bought bread because I was sad," T says this.

108
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:16,760
"What kind of bread did you buy?"

109
00:09:16,760 --> 00:09:20,510
"Why did you buy bread when you were feeling down?"

110
00:09:20,510 --> 00:09:22,570
"Do you like bread?"

111
00:09:22,570 --> 00:09:24,600
"Was it delicious?"

112
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:30,460
On the other hand, F values emotions.

113
00:09:30,460 --> 00:09:33,450
Empathy is important.

114
00:09:33,450 --> 00:09:40,220
A friend says, "I bought bread because I was sad."

115
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:44,480
Then F says this.

116
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,960
"Are you okay?"

117
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:48,030
"It must have been really hard, right?"

118
00:09:48,030 --> 00:09:49,640
"You did well."

119
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:52,340
"Eat the bread and cheer up."

120
00:09:52,340 --> 00:09:54,980
This is F.

121
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:57,720
They are very considerate.

122
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:03,013
They are good at empathizing.

123
00:10:01,080 --> 00:10:05,570
How did you guys answer?

124
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:12,830
There are so many T and F memes in Korea.

125
00:10:12,830 --> 00:10:16,480
There is a buzzword. A slang term.

126
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:18,530
There is a buzzword.

127
00:10:18,530 --> 00:10:24,030
"Are you a T? Are you a T? T?"

128
00:10:24,030 --> 00:10:26,330
People say it like this.

129
00:10:26,330 --> 00:10:32,940
Suppose a friend or family member doesn't empathize with what I say.

130
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:38,210
They hurt my feelings. This is the phrase used in those moments.

131
00:10:38,210 --> 00:10:44,800
I say this to my mom a lot lately.

132
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:53,380
For example, I tell my mom, "I took an exam but I kind of messed it up."

133
00:10:53,380 --> 00:11:02,060
Then my mom says, "Oh well, hurry up and prepare for the next exam."

134
00:11:02,060 --> 00:11:10,460
But I was expecting something like, "You went through a lot... it was hard, wasn't it?"

135
00:11:10,460 --> 00:11:17,100
In those moments, I say, "Oh, Mom, are you a T?"

136
00:11:17,100 --> 00:11:19,020
I'm just joking.

137
00:11:19,020 --> 00:11:23,760
The last ones are J and P.

138
00:11:23,760 --> 00:11:28,540
J likes to plan.

139
00:11:28,540 --> 00:11:33,720
They prepare in advance.

140
00:11:33,720 --> 00:11:39,620
They like organizing.

141
00:11:39,620 --> 00:11:47,800
For example, they make all the plans before going on a trip.

142
00:11:47,800 --> 00:11:50,120
They make them in advance.

143
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:53,160
They even set the time.

144
00:11:53,160 --> 00:11:55,870
They are very meticulous.

145
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:57,150
Meticulous.

146
00:11:57,150 --> 00:11:58,810
Meticulous.

147
00:11:58,810 --> 00:12:02,370
This is J.

148
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:05,730
P likes being free.

149
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:10,080
It's okay even without a plan.

150
00:12:10,080 --> 00:12:16,130
This kind of personality is called "spontaneous" in Korean.

151
00:12:16,130 --> 00:12:17,540
To be spontaneous.

152
00:12:17,540 --> 00:12:23,460
People say, "I am spontaneous."

153
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:33,690
When preparing for a trip, they say, "Let's just think about it then... not now."

154
00:12:33,690 --> 00:12:35,520
This is P.

155
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:41,820
In Korea, people talk about J and P a lot too.

156
00:12:41,820 --> 00:12:51,480
When friends talk about trips, this topic comes up a lot.

157
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:59,810
Now, we combine these letters one by one.

158
00:12:59,810 --> 00:13:02,940
One from E or I.

159
00:13:02,940 --> 00:13:05,950
One from N or S.

160
00:13:05,950 --> 00:13:08,860
One from T or F.

161
00:13:08,860 --> 00:13:11,870
One from J or P.

162
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:15,390
For example, ENTJ.

163
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:20,480
How many letters are there like this?

164
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:22,370
There are four.

165
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:23,760
Four.

166
00:13:23,760 --> 00:13:30,260
That is your MBTI, your personality.

167
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:35,300
Did you guys understand MBTI well?

168
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:42,460
In Korea, MBTI is really popular.

169
00:13:42,460 --> 00:13:43,490
Popularity.

170
00:13:43,490 --> 00:13:49,760
When you meet Korean people later, try saying this.

171
00:13:49,760 --> 00:13:52,740
"What is your MBTI?"

172
00:13:52,740 --> 00:13:55,390
"What's your MBTI?"

173
00:13:55,390 --> 00:14:00,130
When you meet people who are like friends, not older adults.

174
00:14:00,130 --> 00:14:03,150
"What's your MBTI?"

175
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:09,340
Then Korean people will really like it.

176
00:14:09,340 --> 00:14:17,090
You can even see which types get along well like this.

177
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:23,860
Anyway, please review the personality expressions you learned today.

178
00:14:23,860 --> 00:14:30,950
And try talking about your personality in Korean.

179
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:37,810
Then I'll try to guess your MBTI in the comments.

180
00:14:37,810 --> 00:14:50,830
Then, see you next time. Bye!
